    <string name="faq_note_actions_q">What does a long press on a note do?</string>
    <string name="faq_note_actions_a">It opens the note\'s actions: change its tag, add a short description shown on the card, duplicate the note or move it to the trash.</string>
    <string name="faq_trash_q">How do I get a deleted note back?</string>
    <string name="faq_trash_a">Deleted notes go to Trash in the menu. There you can restore a note or delete it forever. Encly never empties the trash on its own.</string>
    <string name="faq_lock_note_q">What does \"Lock editing\" do?</string>
    <string name="faq_lock_note_a">It makes a note read-only so it can\'t be changed by accident. You can still select and copy the text. Turn it on or off from the editor\'s menu.</string>
    <string name="faq_backup_q">How do backups work?</string>
    <string name="faq_backup_a">In Settings → Backup you export one encrypted file that only your recovery phrase can open. To restore, pick the file, type or paste the 12 words, then merge it into this vault or replace everything.</string>
